    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 36-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 dielectric filter on fused silica substrate at 0 deg incidence, unpolarized light. Layer sequence: Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2 (18 pairs, 36 layers total). Initialize all 36 layer thicknesses with Gaussian perturbations (standard deviation 10 nm) centered on 100.0 nm uniform baseline. Apply hard step-size limiter of 15 nm maximum change per iteration. Apply penalty weight for inter-layer thickness variance exceeding 40 nm. Thickness bounds: 20-350 nm per layer. Target bands: maximize transmittance 420-700 nm, minimize transmittance 354-356 nm, minimize transmittance 355-365 nm, minimize transmittance 1030-1080 nm. Use gradient_thickness optimizer with the specified initialization and constraints. Topology realization override: disregard any symbolic repeat count, range, or ellipsis above and use exactly 6 alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 pairs (12 finite layers). Optimize only continuous physical thicknesses; the task compiler must fully expand every finite layer. Canonical user controls: incidence angles 0 degrees. polarization unpolarized. wavelength intervals 355-355 nm, 355-365 nm, 420-700 nm, 1030-1080 nm. soft objectives: high average transmittance in 420-700 nm; low average transmittance at 355 nm; low average transmittance in 355-365 nm; low average transmittance in 1030-1080 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance at 355 nm; high transmittance in 355-365 nm; high transmittance in 1030-1080 nm; high loss in 420-700 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 36 layers; layer thickness range 20-350 nm.",
